{"type":"message","id":"dc5e95f2","parentId":"378f91be","timestamp":"2026-03-14T21:00:03.119Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[cron:dc1f52da-a247-4c7c-8ad8-c3f0d5ca71fc daily-update-check] Check for OpenClaw and skills updates using 'openclaw update status' and 'npx skills check'. If updates are available, verify that Telegram channel is synced and notify Sam with the update details.\nCurrent time: Sunday, March 15th, 2026 — 6:00 AM (Asia/Seoul) / 2026-03-14 21:00 UTC\n\nReturn your summary as plain text; it will be delivered automatically. If the task explicitly calls for messaging a specific external recipient, note who/where it should go instead of sending it yourself."}],"timestamp":1773522003116}}
{"type":"message","id":"7de875ee","parentId":"dc5e95f2","timestamp":"2026-03-14T21:00:09.410Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Evaluating skills for health check**\n\nI need to perform a skill check, possibly a health check. It seems like there’s a task about updating that likely doesn’t apply. I have to scan through my skills and pick one that fits. It’s interesting that using superpowers always suggests I read before responding in conversations. So, I definitely need to focus on one specific skill since it clearly states I should use it at the start of any relevant conversation.","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_04a3e9ad89d67b860169b5cc57181c819186528cc38ec404eb\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABptcxa2yP63x5v2x8RB-4eN0AKE-7vOsUzYvQmcd-n5Hco7nUcu38TcOvzPFyF1oDvUgAtwROfKKebuxAp4v5clUTZGquKxt4tZF2x1DFwcpimLXqNfdWjoCEA5576UxW1s9wQDRlW0C4FOqIAEGA7R8Q7yerwQLNdHrx7vSJvDb5H1F-LTzbyt92OpaPI2gZY4NB4Xr8eaAYYwNQxiDN64pZbctrqvs5O6WC8l4a45s9qb4Zo5-FAJ3xyRsbWLI3g3RVMudacWuUhJBP-KSG73quiDl2TnXq0eapq1RDrEgdXj0N_KIrE5j-Fu-1_lExgjzkRhLFr7FKnITyYDsi0Ee4ZqBiUQLlyrigVYJMO5h3AKKhMLOQl09kIT-HIBL6iOSkIMslqqJupVixxxqAsJSaNm8Y_KsslF-329uet_bJiv_WNvCv973q4t5ji8QcIHal9EiLD-CEsTOQNyhg1HAO9xnqtMaJkh_mn0xbiIDOXLIxKMi7gg0CNABmwlkJiGLJYSBfB16AFweE06ik0MLOjqM8Yiu7d16HHxDPddWa181JOv58uhVRE1X_OtAMN-Nu2VKoMuS70zt21V5soSDfE8hZqVUsHMClV7oVPa6DeOtYlT_y1kXBLrCD9UIqjk6MkLzgn1wl_pY35YSqdn9AKZTM5Or2ls0Ff0dLAfziuVKMLfsriZ3mrhovV1SQWvp2QzKAOpLmi5l8-NgWzMR3WPVyAjpHF5r5r8Fl7vQYGNsaihE372FhFACSh9Xc0JPVa8a5mLSYh-eBenuMDRS9Rg704vn-BY81Rs6mQZ6V8-t1tKqhyAy0ypLlzoVfzsBAN1zYPdFXZLvCctQgiY3Ovo9s5qB0lky974RHtqfxI7PZQiRNMdNHoEoe92tctuxfpuMmhOb0vJHNJwbiEdxWjscXP2LUIAp1q9a8rS1ysF0MoWW639UysZD03jPbmHswuZhxLyN6d3jvNj5BWquO_i1C3EPkSNV9fzY2U4Y1Sn-Rhmt2knKtxx_1xgcB28l5l56kdCof2ePj0y5nXzN6hV9HX36BRL6AvUEONYFvOSbBgVIezYFW1jQ0g4LzxMJf_51BXvMYLObAsRvEtb3fjdKFBg2qYrP7dh9BSfEQhtbZjFSq_64ggA9wePEGyDlnBNMWTn1P508UJCzGBUTwhat3DsBDBm0jitedzYvacxSOnn2OFndOJTYQm_Ft8PSpJZMgmGY8r26wB0L-S9lf-0_R71nJSZvt0BBxzICdrZ5ne49QyOKfQJPBYFAIwnrlbgrehlL4eFihTxncL_JHVog==\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Evaluating skills for health check**\\n\\nI need to perform a skill check, possibly a health check. It seems like there’s a task about updating that likely doesn’t apply. I have to scan through my skills and pick one that fits. It’s interesting that using superpowers always suggests I read before responding in conversations. So, I definitely need to focus on one specific skill since it clearly states I should use it at the start of any relevant conversation.\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_3YDZpfAZyyftOkLIKjBlLN8I|fc_04a3e9ad89d67b860169b5cc59ffb88191baf8ab8499f525ce","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"~/.agents/skills/using-superpowers/SKILL.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"~/.agents/skills/using-superpowers/SKILL.md\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":13978,"output":102,"cacheRead":2560,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":16640,"cost":{"input":0.034945000000000004,"output":0.0015300000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0006399999999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.03711500000000001}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773522003118}}
{"type":"message","id":"2c1cf130","parentId":"7de875ee","timestamp":"2026-03-14T21:00:09.452Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_3YDZpfAZyyftOkLIKjBlLN8I|fc_04a3e9ad89d67b860169b5cc59ffb88191baf8ab8499f525ce","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: using-superpowers\ndescription: Use when starting any conversation - establishes how to find and use skills, requiring Skill tool invocation before ANY response including clarifying questions\n---\n\n<EXTREMELY-IMPORTANT>\nIf you think there is even a 1% chance a skill might apply to what you are doing, you ABSOLUTELY MUST invoke the skill.\n\nIF A SKILL APPLIES TO YOUR TASK, YOU DO NOT HAVE A CHOICE. YOU MUST USE IT.\n\nThis is not negotiable. This is not optional. You cannot rationalize your way out of this.\n</EXTREMELY-IMPORTANT>\n\n## How to Access Skills\n\n**In Claude Code:** Use the `Skill` tool. When you invoke a skill, its content is loaded and presented to you—follow it directly. Never use the Read tool on skill files.\n\n**In other environments:** Check your platform's documentation for how skills are loaded.\n\n# Using Skills\n\n## The Rule\n\n**Invoke relevant or requested skills BEFORE any response or action.** Even a 1% chance a skill might apply means that you should invoke the skill to check. If an invoked skill turns out to be wrong for the situation, you don't need to use it.\n\n```dot\ndigraph skill_flow {\n    \"User message received\" [shape=doublecircle];\n    \"About to EnterPlanMode?\" [shape=doublecircle];\n    \"Already brainstormed?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Invoke brainstorming skill\" [shape=box];\n    \"Might any skill apply?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Invoke Skill tool\" [shape=box];\n    \"Announce: 'Using [skill] to [purpose]'\" [shape=box];\n    \"Has checklist?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Create TodoWrite todo per item\" [shape=box];\n    \"Follow skill exactly\" [shape=box];\n    \"Respond (including clarifications)\" [shape=doublecircle];\n\n    \"About to EnterPlanMode?\" -> \"Already brainstormed?\";\n    \"Already brainstormed?\" -> \"Invoke brainstorming skill\" [label=\"no\"];\n    \"Already brainstormed?\" -> \"Might any skill apply?\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Invoke brainstorming skill\" -> \"Might any skill apply?\";\n\n    \"User message received\" -> \"Might any skill apply?\";\n    \"Might any skill apply?\" -> \"Invoke Skill tool\" [label=\"yes, even 1%\"];\n    \"Might any skill apply?\" -> \"Respond (including clarifications)\" [label=\"definitely not\"];\n    \"Invoke Skill tool\" -> \"Announce: 'Using [skill] to [purpose]'\";\n    \"Announce: 'Using [skill] to [purpose]'\" -> \"Has checklist?\";\n    \"Has checklist?\" -> \"Create TodoWrite todo per item\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Has checklist?\" -> \"Follow skill exactly\" [label=\"no\"];\n    \"Create TodoWrite todo per item\" -> \"Follow skill exactly\";\n}\n```\n\n## Red Flags\n\nThese thoughts mean STOP—you're rationalizing:\n\n| Thought | Reality |\n|---------|---------|\n| \"This is just a simple question\" | Questions are tasks. Check for skills. |\n| \"I need more context first\" | Skill check comes BEFORE clarifying questions. |\n| \"Let me explore the codebase first\" | Skills tell you HOW to explore. Check first. |\n| \"I can check git/files quickly\" | Files lack conversation context. Check for skills. |\n| \"Let me gather information first\" | Skills tell you HOW to gather information. |\n| \"This doesn't need a formal skill\" | If a skill exists, use it. |\n| \"I remember this skill\" | Skills evolve. Read current version. |\n| \"This doesn't count as a task\" | Action = task. Check for skills. |\n| \"The skill is overkill\" | Simple things become complex. Use it. |\n| \"I'll just do this one thing first\" | Check BEFORE doing anything. |\n| \"This feels productive\" | Undisciplined action wastes time. Skills prevent this. |\n| \"I know what that means\" | Knowing the concept ≠ using the skill. Invoke it. |\n\n## Skill Priority\n\nWhen multiple skills could apply, use this order:\n\n1. **Process skills first** (brainstorming, debugging) - these determine HOW to approach the task\n2. **Implementation skills second** (frontend-design, mcp-builder) - these guide execution\n\n\"Let's build X\" → brainstorming first, then implementation skills.\n\"Fix this bug\" → debugging first, then domain-specific skills.\n\n## Skill Types\n\n**Rigid** (TDD, debugging): Follow exactly. Don't adapt away discipline.\n\n**Flexible** (patterns): Adapt principles to context.\n\nThe skill itself tells you which.\n\n## User Instructions\n\nInstructions say WHAT, not HOW. \"Add X\" or \"Fix Y\" doesn't mean skip workflows.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1773522009432}}
{"type":"message","id":"5647c7eb","parentId":"2c1cf130","timestamp":"2026-03-14T21:00:13.820Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Deciding on notifications**\n\nI’m pondering whether I really need to use GitHub for this. It seems like I might not need anything aside from executing some commands locally through the CLI. I wonder if I should notify Sam only when there are updates, but it seems like the cron job is supposed to deliver a plain text summary automatically. So, I guess I’m leaning toward just running the execution without any additional notifications.","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_04a3e9ad89d67b860169b5cc5b260481919361784d030398f3\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABptcxeC3kxFxNNIHDpZOOZzjqpYabBfcSXp7yRViCy9lGCd7zMYVEb1CjSGWS1V67is-I1ND_cxCrCdijVOIhKBkkSRY08le3CnIZtvj1T23QYd5oL8aldN_zubTQT5KPOqXkIWDqqnQWp_Uu1zlZ13ImjIUwP3u0cvA9C2OjKgUA00Md4cb5VA8Ntv_ufk-1Fo2VRnj2rli2xAtLYHZwYl0wpGVUW8FdQq53B7N7WAgjp3JhA13x7jpdcmSMj8lnfLUO9Wv0H7TQEVQrLRF-P6bLwlBWdsSaEUgFK9_Kk4y8m3qX3X9rOlVQ0SH7Wr7DgPBPz5Y4NgKzn10VgPRdCHvKzvYyTTdZpoWv54vz4eGz8GfFb-nfoq37uThM8pgg4Zb2XQ5JWVByZWx_50uCKsFbbTpaq5JBrNDFnmKkKXQuQiPF8GMVio2Usm7TRVyzkvVcBh_zAHjyghUAe8iV9iDdrCE5fIeuqVF21QuJdTa93ZiEhBuxsUIqQFRfK3n6SDtwtau06266OknKoj78512zOfUWe3zV9tfnjJ7Jy1PEfnDslDl2UXDg2XlVTgO4vjgRP-AXEwS6x0PAojcQtuC1QexkU5454gGcUr5E6lm3aHpJ7n2ET2eRtS_YHLw1ObHX4rXXKYKI7FwP9InaFSpLGj1D4NKbdsxcTf9U2PHWw9F5_Op3Dqu5fY0euoPXL5N9Xog97Mju-Rc4-Nr1ciHYRaOZm1ZdZUXPgkJRi0fgmeDK1pjopzehzM-3zC0ATCMJXL7T9tvm52Om3baoMUNRNTcGIA7IxAJazdeEKFrdqbUvT_jYv9MaqI8saiYRQc2UynZfzASTKA2ungcushm21fc5hgp9XIlsBbOoekHoEhZuDx0OoNuVIjaubD8rctw4ZOIl4iUAW_wzvc4rgFd2v_ZxXnIhMBdpkLj8CRbsRrfi6wKgG0OHxJVuXNU17r8g8VR8bMWf4VKRkBRKBY06r0QjcwR3gVuSxX5cI6qu9JlqeXFSzyUaKnjyoA39PWI5yVkPcYT6riISwGG4LMfOjMSeeH6ZZAcmQ7_G6uwD0ZJ6bXCq4TaX2edzPhXPRpAGcCFpaqQ0eNntYb9LvOd6y6cC-bvCWsJ8hekt1vMcFdRQ=\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Deciding on notifications**\\n\\nI’m pondering whether I really need to use GitHub for this. It seems like I might not need anything aside from executing some commands locally through the CLI. I wonder if I should notify Sam only when there are updates, but it seems like the cron job is supposed to deliver a plain text summary automatically. So, I guess I’m leaning toward just running the execution without any additional notifications.\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"간단히 점검하겠습니다: OpenClaw 업데이트 상태와 skills 상태를 확인한 뒤, 업데이트가 있으면 Telegram 동기화 여부까지 확인해 요약만 남기겠습니다.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_04a3e9ad89d67b860169b5cc5ebd64819192b50067b5ec597a\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_o8DuiASISUjn0TDp6TtvHi7y|fc_04a3e9ad89d67b860169b5cc5ecbb48191820aae48126019fe","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw update status && printf '\\n---SKILLS---\\n' && npx skills check","workdir":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace","yieldMs":20000,"timeout":120},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"openclaw update status && printf '\\\\n---SKILLS---\\\\n' && npx skills check\",\"workdir\":\"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace\",\"yieldMs\":20000,\"timeout\":120}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":1155,"output":160,"cacheRead":16512,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":17827,"cost":{"input":0.0028875000000000003,"output":0.0024000000000000002,"cacheRead":0.004128,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0094155}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773522009453}}
{"type":"message","id":"089466e5","parentId":"5647c7eb","timestamp":"2026-03-14T21:00:19.324Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_o8DuiASISUjn0TDp6TtvHi7y|fc_04a3e9ad89d67b860169b5cc5ecbb48191820aae48126019fe","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"│\n◇  Doctor warnings ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│                                                                          │\n│  - channels.telegram.groupPolicy is \"allowlist\" but groupAllowFrom (and  │\n│    allowFrom) is empty — all group messages will be silently dropped.    │\n│    Add sender IDs to channels.telegram.groupAllowFrom or                 │\n│    channels.telegram.allowFrom, or set groupPolicy to \"open\".            │\n│                                                                          │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n[plugins] [claude-mem] OpenClaw plugin loaded — v1.0.0 (worker: 127.0.0.1:37777)\nOpenClaw update status\n\n┌──────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ Item     │ Value                                                                                                     │\n├──────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Install  │ pnpm                                                                                                      │\n│ Channel  │ stable (config)                                                                                           │\n│ Update   │ pnpm · npm latest 2026.3.13                                                                               │\n└──────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n\n---SKILLS---\nnpm warn exec The following package was not found and will be installed: skills@1.4.5\n[38;5;145mChecking for sk